("backpressure", "Bounded ingestion and backpressure", "Backpressure limits work admitted into a saturated service. Bounded queues and concurrency avoid unbounded memory growth. Retrying every rejected request immediately can amplify overload.", "https://sre.google/sre-book/handling-overload/"),
